{"name":"Cheddar","hex":"#ee9a09","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cheddar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large village and civil parish, previously in Sedgemoor district, Somerset, England, famous for its cheese, and also for its gorge, caves and remains of early man found in them .","A ghost town in Highlands East municipality, Haliburton County, Ontario, Canada."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cheddar cheese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cheddar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheddar cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheddar cheese is a natural cheese that is relatively hard, off-white, and sometimes sharp-tasting. It originates from the village of Cheddar in Somerset, South West England."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Somerset-Cheddar.jpg/330px-Somerset-Cheddar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheddar_cheese","wikidata":"Q217525"},{"title":"Cheddar, Somerset","blocks":[{"text":"Cheddar is a large village and civil parish in the English county of Somerset. It is situated on the southern edge of the Mendip Hills, 9 miles (14 km) north-west of Wells, 11 miles (18 km) south-east of Weston-super-Mare and 18 miles (29 km) south-west of Bristol. The civil parish includes the hamlets of Nyland and Bradley Cross. The parish had a population of 5,755 in 2011 and an acreage of 8,592 acres (3,477 ha) as of 1961."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Cheddar_09-06_9.jpg/330px-Cheddar_09-06_9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheddar%2C_Somerset","wikidata":"Q1019479"},{"title":"Cheddar (TV channel)","blocks":[{"text":"Cheddar Inc. is an American live streaming financial news network founded by Jon Steinberg in the United States. Cheddar broadcasts live daily from the floor of the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE), Nasdaq, the Flatiron Building in New York City, and the White House lawn and briefing room in Washington, D.C. covering new products, technologies, and services."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheddar_(TV_channel)","wikidata":"Q28453499"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg/500px-MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg/1280px-MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg/500px-MidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cheddar cheeses on display at the 2003 Mid-Somerset Show","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidSomerset_Show_170803.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cheddar_in_London.png/500px-Cheddar_in_London.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cheddar_in_London.png/1280px-Cheddar_in_London.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Cheddar_in_London.png/500px-Cheddar_in_London.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cylinders of cheddar on display in London, early 20th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheddar_in_London.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Cheese_curds_2.jpg/500px-Cheese_curds_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Cheese_curds_2.jpg/1280px-Cheese_curds_2.jpg?utm_sou